---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { NEIGHBORHOOD, OFFICIAL_ORG_NAME, displayName } from '../lib/site';
import { DEFAULT_SITE_SETTINGS } from '../lib/types';

// Every statement below describes what the code actually does; change the
// page when the data handling changes. The mode-dependent parts follow the
// same `officialMode` switch as /contact: who runs the site, where the contact
// form goes, and the association-business features that exist only then.
const site = Astro.locals.site ?? DEFAULT_SITE_SETTINGS;
const official = site.officialMode;
const name = displayName(site);
const operator = official
  ? `the ${OFFICIAL_ORG_NAME} board`
  : 'the resident who maintains this site';
const EFFECTIVE = '29 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${name} collects, uses, and protects personal information.`}
>
  <div class="page-section policy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Effective {EFFECTIVE}.</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    {official ? (
      <p>
        {`${name} (ashebrookresidents.com) is operated by the ${OFFICIAL_ORG_NAME} board for the homeowners of ${NEIGHBORHOOD}.`}
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        {name} (ashebrookresidents.com) is an independent site run by a resident
        of {NEIGHBORHOOD}. It is not operated by the HOA or its management
        company. In this policy, "we" means {operator}.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

    <h3>When you browse</h3>
    <p>
      You can read the public pages without an account. Like any website, our
      host, Cloudflare, receives your IP address and browser details with each
      request. Cloudflare uses them to deliver the page, protect the site from
      abuse, and keep short-term operational logs. Pages load fonts from Google
      Fonts, so Google also receives your IP address. The calendar page embeds a
      Google Calendar.
    </p>

    <h3>Your account</h3>
    <p>
      To create an account we ask for your name, email address, and a password.
      We store the password only as a one-way hash, never the password itself.
      We email you a link to confirm your address, and another if you ask to
      reset your password. While you are signed in, we keep your session along
      with the IP address and browser it came from, for up to 7 days after your
      last visit.
    </p>

    <h3>Signing in with Google</h3>
    <p>
      If you choose to sign in with Google, we ask Google only for your basic
      profile and email address. We never request access to your Google Drive,
      contacts, or any other Google data. We keep your name, your email address,
      and the identifier Google assigns to your account, so you can sign in
      again. We do not keep Google's access tokens or your profile photo.
      Signing in with Google does not by itself give you homeowner access; that
      still requires verifying your property. You can disconnect Google from
      your Account page at any time.
    </p>

    <h3>Verifying your property</h3>
    <p>
      To unlock homeowner features, you enter your property address and name and
      choose email or text. We compare them with the association's owner
      records. If they match, we send a one-time code to the email address or
      phone number already on those records, not to one you type in. Codes go
      out through Resend (email) or Twilio (text). A Cloudflare Turnstile check,
      which sees your IP address, guards the form against bots. Codes expire
      after 10 minutes and are deleted a day later. If you ask the board to
      review a request instead, that request is deleted 30 days after it is
      resolved. Once you are verified, your account is linked to your owner
      record, and you can unlink it yourself.
    </p>

    <h3>Association records</h3>
    <p>
      The site holds the association's roster: owners' names, lot addresses,
      contact details, ownership history, and board service. These come from the
      association's own records rather than from visitors. Contact details are
      never shown publicly. Board administrators can see the roster, and a
      verified homeowner can see their own record. Some names are public because
      they are part of the association's meeting records, such as board members
      at a meeting, who made or seconded a motion, and election candidates.
    </p>

    {official && (
      <>
        <h3>Voting, proxies, and lot records</h3>
        <p>
          When these features are turned on, we record the proxies homeowners
          grant, including the name of the person holding each proxy, and votes
          on member motions, which are tied to the lot that cast them. The
          record of a public member meeting may show how each property voted. In
          board elections the ballot is secret. We record which lots have voted,
          but store the choices without any link to the lot or person that cast
          them. Lot records, such as covenant matters and dues balances, are
          visible only to that lot's owners and the board.
        </p>
      </>
    )}

    <h3>Messages you send us</h3>
    <p>
      The contact form sends your name, email address, and message from your
      browser to Web3Forms, which forwards them by email to {operator}. The site
      itself does not keep a copy.
    </p>

    <h3>Board tools</h3>
    <p>
      Board administrators can use an AI assistant to search and summarize the
      association's documents. Their questions and the relevant document
      excerpts go to Anthropic to produce an answer. Before anything is sent,
      roster names, contact details, and addresses are replaced with
      placeholders, though this masking is best effort. Documents are indexed
      for search using Cloudflare's AI services. The text of saved reports is
      deleted after 90 days.
    </p>

    <h3>Record of changes</h3>
    <p>
      To keep administration accountable, the site keeps a permanent log of
      administrative actions: who acted, when, and what kind of change it was.
      The log does not keep copies of the personal details that were changed.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use only the cookies the site needs to work. One keeps you signed in,
      for up to 7 days. The other protects a Google sign-in while it is in
      progress and lasts 5 minutes. We use no advertising or tracking cookies.
      Cloudflare may set security cookies to tell people from bots, and it
      counts visits with its Web Analytics service, which does not use cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>How we share information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal information or use it for advertising. We share it
      only with the service providers named above to run the site (Cloudflare,
      Google, Resend, Twilio, Web3Forms, and Anthropic), or when the law
      requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Google user data</h2>
    <p>
      Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere
      to the{' '}
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">
        Google API Services User Data Policy
      </a>
      , including the Limited Use requirements. We use Google account
      information only to sign you in to this site.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sessions: up to 7 days after your last visit.</li>
      <li>Verification codes: deleted about a day after they expire.</li>
      <li>Resolved review requests: 30 days.</li>
      <li>Saved board report text: 90 days.</li>
      <li>
        Accounts, association records, and meeting and voting records: for as
        long as the site serves the association.
      </li>
      <li>The administrative change log: permanently.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reset your password from the sign-in page.</li>
      <li>Disconnect Google from your Account page.</li>
      <li>Unlink your account from your owner record.</li>
      <li>
        Ask us, through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, to correct your
        information or close your account. We will do what we can and tell you
        about anything we must keep, such as the change log or voting records.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served only over HTTPS. Passwords are hashed. Each page and
      document is shown only to the visitors allowed to see it. No website is
      perfectly secure, but we work to protect the information we hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is meant for adult residents. It is not directed to children
      under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we will update this page and its effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your information? Use the{' '}
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
